{
  "changelog": "geoskill-hyperspectral-unmixing 1.0.0 \u2013 Initial release\n\n- Supports VCA and N-FINDR endmember extraction algorithms for hyperspectral imagery.\n- Performs linear spectral unmixing using non-negative least squares (nnls) with sum-to-one abundance normalization.\n- Outputs include abundance maps, residual RMSE maps, extracted endmember spectra (JSON), and a manifest file.\n- Works fully offline; supports both synthetic (generated) data and real hyperspectral GeoTIFF input.\n- Installation via pip: numpy, rasterio, scipy.",
